stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've repaired the network by hand. It changes 345 of 7428 parameters (limit 371), and `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are in place.\n\n**What was going wrong:** in 2 of the 6 recorded start-network episodes, cars stuck in the invisible W2 pocket were never served. The network sat in EW-through until the 90-minute cap. During the hour, W2 also overflowed and blocked the upstream lane it shares with W through traffic.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Stand-in input (column 5 of W1):** q_E2 now also feeds the weights for q_W2 and d_W2. E2 has the same demand and the same phase.\n- **Idle detector (layer-1 unit 4, repurposed):** on when nothing is visible except cars halted on W1u.\n- **Blockage detector (layer-1 unit 28):** on when EW-through is green and a car halts on W1u. On the visible sides, this means the left pocket is full 98–100% of the time.\n- **Relay (layer-2 unit 37):** passes those two signals into the EW-left logit only.\n\n**Checks (forward passes only):**\n- Each detector fires only on its intended recorded states.\n- All recorded deadlock and empty-tail states now pick EW-left.\n- Synthetic idle states pick EW-left with a margin of at least 3 logits.\n- In blockage states, decisions match the original net seeing W2 full 95% of the time.\n- Everywhere else, 99.5% of decisions match the original net fed the E2 stand-in.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h), estimated without any simulation:** low 35.1, nominal 45.6, high 56.8.","ttft_ms":2795,"type":"result","duration_ms":1063321,"uuid":"b3f5d79a-f9c1-4407-9734-68ffac9aaea7","ttft_stream_ms":2312,"time_to_request_ms":56,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":